      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "We have the system of equations:\n\\begin{align*}\n4u - 5v &= 23, \\\\\n2u + 4v &= -8.\n\\end{align*}\n\nFirst, we will eliminate one of the variables. We can multiply the second equation by 2 to get:\n\\begin{align*}\n4u - 5v &= 23, \\\\\n4u + 8v &= -16.\n\\end{align*}\n\nNow, we subtract the second equation from the first equation to eliminate $u$:\n\\begin{align*}\n(4u - 5v) - (4u + 8v) &= 23 - (-16), \\\\\n4u - 5v - 4u - 8v &= 23 + 16, \\\\\n-13v &= 39.\n\\end{align*}\n\nSolving for $v$, we get:\n\\begin{align*}\nv &= \\frac{39}{-13} = -3.\n\\end{align*}\n\nNow that we have $v$, we can substitute it back into one of the original equations to solve for $u$. We will use the first equation:\n\\begin{align*}\n4u - 5(-3) &= 23, \\\\\n4u + 15 &= 23, \\\\\n4u &= 8, \\\\\nu &= \\frac{8}{4} = 2.\n\\end{align*}\n\nNow that we have both $u$ and $v$, we can find $u+v$:\n\\begin{align*}\nu + v &= 2 + (-3), \\\\\nu + v &= -1.\n\\end{align*}\n\nTherefore, the value of $u+v$ is $\\boxed{-1}$.",
