    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve the system of linear equations\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n4u - 5v = 23 \\\\\n2u + 4v = -8\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\nwe can use the method of elimination or substitution. Here, we'll use the elimination method.\n\nFirst, we'll multiply the second equation by 2 to align the coefficients of \\(u\\):\n\n\\[\n2 \\times (2u + 4v = -8) \\rightarrow 4u + 8v = -16\n\\]\n\nNow we have the system:\n\\[\n\\begin{cases}\n4u - 5v = 23 \\\\\n4u + 8v = -16\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nNext, we'll subtract the first equation from the second equation to eliminate \\(u\\):\n\n\\[\n(4u + 8v) - (4u - 5v) = -16 - 23\n\\]\n\nThis simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n4u + 8v - 4u + 5v = -39\n\\]\n\n\\[\n13v = -39\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\(v\\):\n\n\\[\nv = \\frac{-39}{13}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nv = -3\n\\]\n\nNow that we have \\(v\\), we substitute it back into one of the original equations to find \\(u\\). Let's use the first equation:\n\n\\[\n4u - 5(-3) = 23\n\\]\n\n\\[\n4u + 15 = 23\n\\]\n\nSubtract 15 from both sides:\n\n\\[\n4u = 8\n\\]\n\nDivide by 4:\n\n\\[\nu = 2\n\\]\n\nFinally, we need to find \\(u + v\\):\n\n\\[\nu + v = 2 + (-3) = -1\n\\]\n\nSo the value of \\(u + v\\) is \\boxed{-1}.",
